  "description": "Faithful in-memory IStorage<T> for Unified.Data.Tables: rows round-trip through the real TableEntitySerializer (so tests exercise production serialization behavior — decimal-as-double, enum-as-string, nested flattening, oversized cells, lossless [TableValueSplit] large values with an in-memory blob store for offload), with the service's semantics through the provider-neutral exceptions TableStorage<T> throws (DuplicateKeyException on a duplicate create, ConcurrencyConflictException on an ETag conflict, EntityNotFoundException for a missing row), the service's status and error code kept as the InnerException, per-transaction batches, QueryOptions.Select projection, and identical id normalization and key splitting. For unit tests, dev mode, and offline runtime.",
